            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lilygloves"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fabulous! I double the recipe (2.5 tsp yeast) for my 2 lb bread machine. The bread is wonderful the next day, too!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kat Mooney"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I really like this recipe, it's a staple at our house.\n\nA couple of modifications: \n\n- I always double the recipe and don't bake it in the bread machine. The machine just takes care of the kneading/rising etc. but the actual baking takes place in the oven on a pre-heated pizza stone. \n- I don't use any type of milk/milk powder. We all agreed that it made the bread too sweet\n- instead of butter, we use olive oil\n- I also add dry rosemary and a shot glass of whatever grains we have floating around \n- I also add a bit more salt, otherwise, it was just a tad too sweet for our liking.\n\nAll in all, a fantastic starting point of a recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-21T16:55:08.810Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "2"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "steph"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I, like one of the other bakers, had a problem with it only turning out about 2 inches high. This was the first bread machine recipe that I measured out the 1 1/2 tsp of dry yeast instead of just putting the whole pack of yeast in. I think if I would have added the pack it would have turned out nicely.",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-02T13:49:43.063Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MOMMIESAPP"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved it! its a perfect recipe to throw into the bread machine. And heres a tip: when using the dry milk, substitute fresh milk for the amount of water called for, and don't use water. It makes the bread sweeter!",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-05T05:20:06.797Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FrackFamily5 CACT"
            },
            "reviewBody": "THIS DID MAKE A SMALLER THAN \"NORMAL\" LOAF IN MY BREAD MACHINE. I WAS WORRIED THAT IT WOULD COME OUT SHORT SO I ADDED YEAST TO MAKE 2.25 TSPS. THE FLAVOR WAS REALLY GOOD AND I BAKED IT ON THE MED DARKNESS SO THE CRUST WAS EXTRA CRUNCHY. MADE THIS LOAF TO GO WITH STUFFED SHELLS AND THERE WAS NONE LEFT. VERY GOOD!",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-19T12:28:07.667Z"
          },
          {
